## `encoding-hints`

Report non-ASCII text in field values as hints when checking compatibility with legacy BibTeX toolchains, which may mishandle UTF-8 during sorting, case conversion, or name abbreviation. Unicode-aware consumers, including Biber and website bibliography processors, can accept UTF-8 directly. pdfLaTeX has defaulted to UTF-8 input since April 2018, although supported characters still depend on LaTeX definitions and fonts. This rule does not infer the consumer or detect an actual encoding incompatibility. Enable it with `extend-select = ["encoding-hints"]` under `[lint]` for a compatibility audit. No autofix is offered because the right change depends on the project's toolchain.

This rule is **disabled by default**; enable it with `select`.

An accented name entered as raw UTF-8:

```bib
@article{erdos47, author = {Erdős, Paul}}
```

```text
help: encoding-hints
 --> references.bib:1:32
  |
1 | @article{erdos47, author = {Erdős, Paul}}
  |                                ^ non-ASCII text `ő`; legacy BibTeX toolchains may mishandle UTF-8; check compatibility or use a LaTeX escape
```
